  <item>
    <title>14.轻重强弱</title>
    <link>https://www.xiaoyuzhoufm.com/episode/65d202390847349e0c562deb</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">65d202390847349e0c562deb</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 18 Feb 2024 13:12:23 +0000</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><span>**本期口播🎙️：** 爸爸的机器人小哥哥🤖</span></p><span></span><p><span>**本期简介📄：** 怎么学好英语，就是"用"！💬📚✨</span></p><span></span><p><span>---</span></p><span></span><p><strong><span>讲述中英文语音魅力：音节、声调和停顿的秘密</span></strong></p><span></span><p><span>你知道中英文发音有哪些迷人之处吗？今天，咱们就一起研究中英文的基础构成单位——音节。我们的字字珠玑，在发音方式、节奏调性上与英语有何不同呢？学外语时携带母语口音未必就是件坏事，不过了解中英文音节的魅力，能帮你说得更地道。例如，强读变化如何塑造发音的节奏？口语中的速读、同化现象又是怎样的？跟着我的播客，让我们一起拨开语音的迷雾，找到语言学习中的航标。</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="137">00:02:17</a>:多国语言中，语音处理方式的相似之处与细微差异。</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="257">00:04:17</a>:如何准确读出重音和次重音？音高、语速和重音位置的影响！</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="377">00:06:17</a>:英语发音中的强读与弱读现象及影响分析</span></p><span></span><p><span><a class="timestamp" data-timestamp="499">00:08:19</a>:揭秘英语中的弱读与强读现象：背后的奥秘是什么？</span></p><span></span><p><span>---</span></p><span></span><p><strong><span>最常见最普及的强读式、弱读式对照列表</span></strong></p><span></span><p><span>- a: /eɪ/→/ə/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- am: /æm/→/əm, m/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- an: /æn/→/ən, n/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- and: /ænd/→/ənd, nd, ən, n/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- any: /'eni/→/ni/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- are: /a:/→/ə/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- as: /æs/→/əz/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- at: /æt/→/ət/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- but: /bʌt/→/bət/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- can: /kæn/→/kən, kn, kŋ/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- could: /kud/→/kəd, kd/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- do: /duː/→/du, də, d/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- does: /dʌz/→/dəz, z, s/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- for: /fɔː/→/fə/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- from: /frɔm/→/frəm, frm/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- had: /hæd/→/həd, əd, d/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- has: /hæz/→/həz, əz, z, s/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- have: /hæv/→/həv, əv, v/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- he: /hiː/→/hi, iː, i/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- her: /həː/→/hə, əː, ə/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- him: /him/→/im/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- his: /hiz/→/iz/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- I: /ai/→/aː, ə/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- is: /iz/→/s, z/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- many: /'meni/→/mni/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- me: /miː/→/mi/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- must: /mʌst/→/məst, məs/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- my: /mai/→/mi/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- of: /əv/→/əv, v, ə/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- our: /ɑʊɚ/→/ar/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- shall: /ʃæl/→/ʃəl, ʃl/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- she: /ʃiː/→/ʃi/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- should: /ʃud/→/ʃəd, ʃd, ʃt/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- so: /səʊ/→/sə/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- some: /sʌm/→/səm, sm/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- such: /sʌʧ/→/səʧ/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- than: /ðæn/→/ðən, ðn/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- that: /ðæt/→/ðət/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- the: /ði:/→/ði, ðə/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- them: /ðem/→/ðəm, ðm, əm, m/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- then: /ðen/→/ðən/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- to: /tuː/→/tu, tə/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- us: /us/→/əs/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- was: /wɔz/→/wəz, wə/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- we: /wiː/→/wi/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- were: /wəː/→/wə/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- when: /wen/→/wən/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- will: /wil/→/əl, l/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- would: /wud/→/wəd, əd, d/</span></p><span></span><p><span>- you: /juː/→/ju/</span></p>]]></description>
